[{"code":"list_may_be_shared","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":14,"col":30},"end":{"line":14,"col":52}},"title":"LIST MAY BE SHARED","message":"`List.append` changes `taps` in place, and the checker cannot show that nothing\nelse still holds the list.\n\n12|want k t d =\n            ^ `d#Dict.0#Node.2.1` keeps the list here\n13|    ( first, taps ) = Maybe.withDefault (Dict.get d k) ( 0, [] )\n                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `d#Dict.0#Node.2.1` may hold the list through this call\n14|    Dict.insert d k ( first, List.append taps [ t ] )\n                   ^ `d#Dict.0#Node.2.1` is taken here, and read after the change\n                                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the list is changed in place here\n\nTo be safe, change a copy:\n\n14|    Dict.insert d k ( first, List.append (List.copy taps) [ t ] )\n\nThis is a limit of the checker, not proof of sharing: d#Dict.0#Node.2.1 may hold\nit through the call at 13:23, and is read at 14:5."},{"code":"list_may_be_shared","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":24,"col":27},"end":{"line":24,"col":39}},"title":"LIST MAY BE SHARED","message":"`Main.want` changes `old#Dict.0#Node.2.1` in place, and the checker cannot show\nthat nothing else still holds the list.\n\n23|                old = Dict.insert (Dict.insert Dict.empty 1 ( 0, taps )) 2 ( 0, taps )\n                   ^^^ `old#Dict.0#Node.2.1` keeps the list here\n                                      ^^^^^^^^^^^ `old#Dict.0#Node.2.1` may hold the list through this call\n24|                changed = want 1 2 old\n                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^ the list is changed in place here\n25|                ( size changed 1, size changed 2, size old 1 )\n                                                          ^^^ and `old#Dict.0#Node.2.1` is read here, after the change\n\nCopy the list with `List.copy` before it is changed, so the change cannot reach\nanything else that holds it.\n\nThis is a limit of the checker, not proof of sharing: old#Dict.0#Node.2.1 may\nhold it through the call at 23:36, and is read at 25:51."}]
